From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 16:21:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/9] The Join button carries a ticket, and a room is switched
 on from Departments
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The app's side of the lesson room. EXPO_PUBLIC_ROOM_URL names the room's
host; empty means the platform is off in that build and every online
session keeps its Zoom link. A session whose meeting_url sits on that host
joins on a single-use ticket from room-ticket, opened in the in-app browser
sheet; the breakout caption and the office's override controls are hidden
for it, since the one thing they can do to a room link is clear it away.
If the room cannot be reached the centre's Zoom link opens instead; if the
room refuses this person, its sentence is shown and nothing else opens.

The teacher's Write tab lists online lessons a fortnight each way from
my_online_lessons, with Join inside the lesson's window and the report's
state once it is over. Account → Departments gains a "Lesson platform"
On / Off per room, drawn only on a build that knows the room's address.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016Yf774TAZaYcnfPt2CdeHJ
